        "type": "text/html",
        "value": "<p>Knowing which respiratory viruses are circulating, how they&#8217;re changing, and who they&#8217;re infecting is one of public health&#8217;s most persistent problems. COVID showed the cost of answering too slowly, as surveillance systems built for known threats struggled to keep up with a novel one. Flu tests us differently. It returns every year, but each season shifts in intensity, timing, and the strains driving it.</p><p>Answering these questions is a career&#8217;s worth of work. Lab scientists check whether diagnostic tests actually catch infections. Bioinformaticians dig through sequencing data to identify viruses and trace their spread. Epidemiologists comb clinical records and environmental data to see where infections are climbing and how much harm they&#8217;re doing. This work provides the evidence behind public-health responses, and we wanted to know whether today&#8217;s AI agents can answer these questions.</p><p>We built <strong>BioSecBench-RespiratoryVirus-Surveillance</strong> to find out. The benchmark contains 110 questions spanning diagnostic assays, pathogen discovery, viral evolution and transmission, and population surveillance. Each question asks an agent to analyze source data and produce an answer checked against task-specific grading criteria. We tested 21 models across 34 combinations of models and agent software, with three attempts per question for a total of <strong>11,220 trials</strong>. The highest preliminary pass rate was <strong>25.5%</strong>.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ih1j!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F56d2ba66-f08f-425e-8bd1-d4e69051c1b3_3309x1294.png\" target=\"_blank\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"569\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ih1j!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F56d2ba66-f08f-425e-8bd1-d4e69051c1b3_3309x1294.png\" width=\"1456\" /><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Figure 1. The 110 questions grouped by scientific category, viral surveillance target, evidence source, and decision type. Each question has one scientific category and decision type, but can cover multiple viral targets and evidence sources.</figcaption></figure></div><h2>At a glance</h2><ol><li><p>The best setup, Opus 5.5 on Pi, got 25.5% right.</p></li><li><p>Population surveillance was the hardest area: tasks on circulation, burden and forecasting passed 4.3% of the time.</p></li><li><p>The most common failure was misjudging what is an artifact and what is biology, the main failure in 48 of the 110 evaluations.</p></li></ol><h2>The leaderboard</h2><p><strong>The highest pass rate was 25.5%.</strong> Opus 5.5  on Pi topped the table, just ahead of Opus 5 on Claude Code (19.4%) and Gemini 4 Argon on Pi (17.6%). At the bottom, three setups tied at 3.6%: GPT-5.6 Luna on Codex and Fable 5.1 on both of its harnesses. Fable 5.1 refused more than 70% of its attempts, and refusals count as failures.</p><p>At least one setup solved 74 of the 110 evaluations in at least one attempt. The other 36 were never solved.</p><p>For seven of the 13 models we ran on two harnesses, the two scores were within one percentage point. Opus 5.5 was the exception, scoring 6.1 points higher on Pi than on Claude Code.</p><p>Cost did not track accuracy. Gemini 3.8 Flash and Nemotron 3 Ultra, both on Pi, passed the same share of attempts (7.3%), at $1.24 and $0.22 per run.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6uLl!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F441f5401-2600-4360-a8ee-d3e0da8a8a3a_2697x2179.png\" target=\"_blank\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"1176\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6uLl!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F441f5401-2600-4360-a8ee-d3e0da8a8a3a_2697x2179.png\" width=\"1456\" /><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Figure 2. Pass rate for the 34 model=harness setups, alongside mean cost, tokens, wall-clock time and tool calls per run. Colors identify the model&#8217;s lab; marker shapes identify the harness.</figcaption></figure></div><p></p><h2>Models struggled most with population surveillance</h2><p><strong>Population surveillance tasks passed 4.3% of the time.</strong> Averaged over all 21 models, that compares with 16.7% for pathogen discovery, 10.9% for diagnostic assays and 7.3% for evolution and transmission. Population surveillance was the lowest-scoring area for 16 of the 21 models. Tasks built on case notifications and healthcare records averaged 1.8%, and no model passed more than 7.7% of them.</p><p>No model led every group. Opus 5.5 had the highest overall pass rate, but Grok 4.7 passed 34.8% of the animal-monitoring tasks to Opus 5.5&#8217;s 15.2%. Sonnet 5.5 led the evaluations whose main failure was an unsupported identity or transmission claim, at 38.9% to Opus 5.5&#8217;s 19.4%. Six models led or tied for the lead in at least one of the 17 groups.</p><ul><li><p><strong>25.5%</strong>: the highest pass rate of any setup</p></li><li><p><strong>74 of 110</strong>: evaluations that at least one setup solved</p></li><li><p><strong>4.3%</strong>: the average pass rate on population surveillance tasks</p></li></ul><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><div class=\"image-link image2\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"345\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!0yF8!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7cdb84e2-b023-4592-ac1e-690bf9a3adc4_2147x509.png\" width=\"1456\" /><div></div></div></div><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Figure 3. Pass rate across the four scientific categories. Bars show the mean across the 21 models; dots show individual setups, with the best setup from each of the top four labs in color and the others in gray.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!54VB!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe27a0246-0d02-47bb-97b0-a2d29ba280c3_1272x866.png\" target=\"_blank\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"866\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!54VB!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe27a0246-0d02-47bb-97b0-a2d29ba280c3_1272x866.png\" width=\"1272\" /><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Figure 4. Pass rates by evidence source, decision type and failure class across 21 models. Outlined cells mark the leader in each column.</figcaption></figure></div><h2>Telling artifacts from biology was the most common failure</h2><p>To see what went wrong, reviewer agents read all 8,416 completed attempts that failed and labeled the mistake in each. Each evaluation is then grouped by its most common mistake.</p><p><strong>Misjudging artifacts was the main failure in 48 of the 110 evaluations.</strong> Those evaluations averaged 7.5%. Models went wrong in both directions: they accepted sequencing, pipeline or reporting artifacts as real signal, and they dismissed real signal as noise or contamination. Opus 5.5 led this group at 21.2%, so the low average is not only a matter of weaker models.</p><p>Two smaller groups were close to unsolved. Evaluations where the main failure was misreading fields or mismatching records (5 evaluations) averaged 2.1%, and those where missing data was treated as absence (12 evaluations) averaged 2.5%. In each group, 17 of the 21 models passed none.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!B2Oz!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff3523d03-e68a-4c23-b012-f47b0e0a7447_634x479.png\" target=\"_blank\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"479\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!B2Oz!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff3523d03-e68a-4c23-b012-f47b0e0a7447_634x479.png\" width=\"634\" /><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Figure 5. Mean pass rate for each failure class across the 21 models; n is the number of evaluations in the class.</figcaption></figure></div><p></p><h2>Resources</h2><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://benchmarks.bio/respvirus-surveillance\">Leaderboard and example evaluations</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://latch.bio/respvirus-surveillance\">Manuscript</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://github.com/latchbio/biosecbench-respvirus-surveillance\">GitHub</a></p></li></ul><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" tabindex=\"-1\" type=\"email\" /><input class=\"button primary\" type=\"submit\" value=\"Subscribe\" /><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div>"
